@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About | Character Chronicles</PageTitle>

<section class="holder-page about-page">

    <div class="holder-symbol"
         aria-hidden="true">
        CC
    </div>

    <div class="holder-shell about-shell">

        <div class="about-copy">

            <p class="holder-eyebrow">
                About the Chronicle
            </p>

            <h1>
                Every Hero Deserves
                <br />
                <span>A Story Worth Keeping</span>
            </h1>

            <p class="holder-intro">
                Character Chronicles is a Dungeons & Dragons
                5th Edition companion designed to help players
                create, organize, and maintain the characters
                that bring their adventures to life.
            </p>

            <div class="about-values">

                <article>
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved"
                       aria-hidden="true"></i>

                    <div>
                        <h2>Built for Players</h2>

                        <p>
                            Create characters, roll ability scores,
                            maintain character sheets, and keep your
                            adventurers ready for the next session.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-compass"
                       aria-hidden="true"></i>

                    <div>
                        <h2>Designed to Grow</h2>

                        <p>
                            The application is structured to support
                            campaigns, Dungeon Master tools, custom
                            character metrics, and additional character
                            systems as development continues.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </article>

            </div>

            <a class="holder-primary"
               href="/characters">
                Explore Characters
            </a>

        </div>

        <aside class="about-panel">

            <div class="about-rings"
                 aria-hidden="true">
            </div>

            <i class="fa-solid fa-dice-d20"
               aria-hidden="true"></i>

            <strong>
                Character Chronicles
            </strong>

            <span>
                Every hero has a story
            </span>

        </aside>

    </div>

    <div class="holder-shell about-details">

        <section class="about-detail-section">

            <p class="holder-eyebrow">
                What We Built
            </p>

            <h2>
                From the first roll to the final chapter
            </h2>

            <div class="feature-grid">

                <article class="feature-card">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-dice"
                       aria-hidden="true"></i>

                    <h3>Roll Ability Scores</h3>

                    <p>
                        Generate six scores using 4d6,
                        discard the lowest die, and assign
                        the results to your character's
                        six core abilities.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="feature-card">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-scroll"
                       aria-hidden="true"></i>

                    <h3>Manage Character Sheets</h3>

                    <p>
                        Edit character information including
                        class, level, background, hit points,
                        personality, ideals, bonds, flaws,
                        equipment, and traits.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="feature-card">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-book-open"
                       aria-hidden="true"></i>

                    <h3>Keep a Persistent Roster</h3>

                    <p>
                        Characters are stored in PostgreSQL
                        and loaded into a reusable character
                        library whenever you return.
                    </p>
                </article>

            </div>

        </section>

        <section class="about-detail-section team-section">

            <p class="holder-eyebrow">
                Development Team
            </p>

            <h2>
                The party behind the project
            </h2>

            <div class="team-grid">

                <article class="team-member">
                    <span>KB</span>
                    <strong>Kevin Bezerra</strong>
                </article>

                <article class="team-member">
                    <span>NS</span>
                    <strong>Nathaniel Stokes</strong>
                </article>

                <article class="team-member">
                    <span>SA</span>
                    <strong>Samuel Apusiyine Avike</strong>
                </article>

                <article class="team-member">
                    <span>VR</span>
                    <strong>Vinicius Eduardo Rocca</strong>
                </article>

                <article class="team-member">
                    <span>JB</span>
                    <strong>Jayce Odin Nephi Brown</strong>
                </article>

            </div>

        </section>

        <section class="about-detail-section roadmap-section">

            <p class="holder-eyebrow">
                The Road Ahead
            </p>

            <h2>
                The chronicle is still being written
            </h2>

            <p>
                Character Chronicles is designed with room
                for future campaign tools, ancestry features,
                class-specific statistics, Dungeon Master
                organization, and custom character metrics.
            </p>

        </section>

    </div>

</section>